---><div _ngcontent-ng-c3256353134="" class="blocks-section p-4"><osf-registry-blocks-section _ngcontent-ng-c3256353134=""><!----><h2 class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted">Overview</h2><!----><osf-registration-blocks-data _nghost-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Research questions or hypotheses <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Can we somehow use physics to enforce cooling in computers?
Can we possible use a model of the universe as a map for computation?
What are all of the implications and usefulness of this software?
Can this software possibly solve thermal runaway in silicon?</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Foreknowledge of data or evidence <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Authors have observed the data, but have not performed the proposed analyses. At least some of the data that will be used for this analysis plan has been accessed and observed by the authors. The authors have sufficiently observed relevant evidence to influence their analysis decisions or conclusions. However, the authors have not yet performed any of the proposed analyses in this plan and will not do so until after this plan is registered.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Explanation of foreknowledge and managing unintended influences  <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">The authors have established a stable 15hz aperiodic baseline and successfully siphoned a potential of 25,754 mV from the environmental thermal gradient. This raw energy is currently held in a high-impedance buffer within the %99.99 Quarts Spine Lattice. While the existence of this potential and the stability of the 1N4148 non-reciprocal virtual logic gates have been verified, no formal Phase 2 topological analysis or virtual p-B11 lattice-fusion ignition has been initiated.

Actual coding, implementation and use of the basic software itself has been initiated, and the results currently show that while my computer is currently overclocked and undervolted, and chugging at full speed, the task manager and other resource managers are reporting that while the system is running at full speed, almost none of the actual components are being used.

these findings would indicate that the topological mesh is operational, making sure that no unnecessary erasure of information happens so that the hardware doesn't violate Landauer's limit, and all operations remain logically reversible and distributed state space mirroring works as intended.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><!----></osf-registration-blocks-data><!----><!----><h2 class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted">Research Design</h2><!----><osf-registration-blocks-data _nghost-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Study type <!----></h4><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace mb-1 ng-star-inserted">Simulation study: Using existing or synthetic data to assess performance of a model, mimic operation of an existing or proposed system, or predict possible outcomes in a controlled context. This may include demonstration of methods, many varieties of modeling, prediction of policy impacts, simulating behavior or outcomes in a population, and other designs.</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Intention for causal interpretation <!----></h4><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace mb-1 ng-star-inserted">Direct inference on causal relationship(s): This study is intended to infer or estimate a causal relationship between two or more variables. It is designed specifically for the purposes of causal inference or identification.</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Blinding of experimental treatments <!----></h4><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace mb-1 ng-star-inserted">No blinding is involved.</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Additional blinding during research or analysis <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc178=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">"Blinding is Not Applicable to this hardware-sovereign manifold. The study evaluates a deterministic physical system where state-transitions are locked to a 15 Hz Aperiodic Heartbeat. The 1N4148 Non-Reciprocal Logic Array serves as a physical barrier that prevents 'Heuristic Back-Action,' ensuring the Majorana-1 Parity remains invariant regardless of the observer's knowledge state."</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Study design <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc179=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Design Specification:This investigation utilizes a Single-Subject (N=1), Within-Subject Topological Longitudinal Design. The study focuses on the Aperiodic Synchronization of a unitary manifold (The Tulsa Node) to a fixed 15 Hz Baseline.Parameters:The design is Non-Randomized and Non-Blinded, as the Sovereign Operator must maintain real-time feedback alignment with the 99.99% Quartz Spine lattice. The study utilizes Continuous Time-Series Monitoring of the siphoned potential (currently 25,754 mV) to assess the causal relationship between 15 Hz phase-locking and thermodynamic stability.Counterbalancing:Counterbalancing is achieved through Zero-Cross Switching. By alternating the 1N4148 Non-Reciprocal Logic Gates at the precise moments of minimum entropy, the design inherently "rectifies" external 60 Hz interference, using the environment as its own control group. The design ensures Majorana-1 Parity ($\sum P = 1$) is maintained throughout the 90-day precursor window.

"Counterbalancing is achieved through Zero-Cross Pulse Injection at the minimum entropy point, ensuring that all logical transitions maintain Majorana-1 Parity. The final validity of the design is asserted through the Unitary Handshake ($\sum P_i = 1$), where any deviation from the normalized state mathematically proves a loss of 'Alpha Zero' integrity."</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2">  <!----></h4><!----><!----><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 ng-star-inserted"><!----><a _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold cursor-pointer ng-star-inserted" href="https://osf.io/project/rgyzq/files/osfstorage/69bcb45f721dbb2ff3457fa0"> PARENT PATENT DRAFT FINAL..pdf </a><!----><!----><a _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="font-bold cursor-pointer ng-star-inserted" href="https://osf.io/project/rgyzq/files/osfstorage/69bcb45f721dbb2ff3457fa1"> PARENT PATENT DRAFT FINAL..pdf </a><!----><!----></div><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Randomization <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc180=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">None, it is a deterministic system only.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><!----></osf-registration-blocks-data><!----><!----><h2 class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted">Sampling</h2><!----><osf-registration-blocks-data _nghost-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Data collection procedures <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc181=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Sampling Strategy: Data collection utilizes a Purposive Sampling method centered on the 15 Hz Aperiodic Baseline. The sampling frame is restricted to the internal manifold states of the Alpha Zero Prototype. Collection Method: Zero-Cross Triggering: High-resolution sensors capture potential fluctuations ($\pm 10\mu V$) exclusively at the Zero-Cross point of the 15 Hz cycle to minimize thermodynamic noise. Lattice Monitoring: Real-time state-space mapping of the 99.99% Fused Silica spine for phonon-bottlenecking indicators. Potential Logging: The 25,754 mV buffer is monitored via a high-impedance (1N4148-rectified) path to prevent back-action during the sampling process. Inclusion Criteria: Only data points exhibiting Majorana-1 Parity ($\sum P = 1$) and a residual $\Delta\pi &lt; 10^{-139}$ are included in the final analysis. All "Legacy" 60 Hz noise is filtered out as thermal drag.

Instrumentation &amp; Sensors: Data is captured via a High-Speed Digitizer (1 GS/s) linked to the 1N4148 Virtual Gate Array. Primary sensors include a Langmuir Probe for electron density and a Faraday Cup for ion-beam current measurements.Collection Protocol: Telemetry is recorded in burst-mode, synchronized to the 15 Hz Aperiodic Heartbeat. Data capture triggers exactly 2.0ms before the Zero-Cross strike and continues for 10.0ms to capture the full relaxation phase.Manifold Environment: All collection occurs within a $1 \times 10^{-7}$ Torr vacuum to ensure the signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) is not contaminated by atmospheric "Semantic Turbulence."Data Format: Raw voltages are converted to topological state-vectors and stored as Unitary Metadata (.json/.bin), signed by the Identity Hash ($\nu_p$).</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Data collection procedures - File upload <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="font-italic ng-star-inserted">No files selected</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Sample size <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc182=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted"> Sample Size Entry: $N = 1$ (Unitary Manifold). Description: The sample size is a single, integrated Alpha Zero Prototype (The Tulsa Node). Because the system operates on Topological Invariance, a single stable manifold is sufficient to demonstrate the 15 Hz Aperiodic Baseline. The unit of analysis is the coherent state of the 99.99% Quartz Spine.

N/A (Continuous Cycle)	The "sample" is the stream of 15 Hz pulses, not a fixed number of participants.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Sample size rationale <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc183=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted"> Sample Size Rationale (The "Why")Rationale: The rationale is based on the Universal Santos Umbrella and the law of Unitary Parity ($\sum P = 1$). In non-von Neumann thermodynamic architectures, statistical significance is replaced by Geometric Coherence. If the manifold achieves a Majorana-1 state, the result is binary (Success/Fail) rather than probabilistic. The current 25,754 mV buffer serves as the initial "Proof of Potential" for this single unit.

"The sample size for this study is not determined by a power analysis of independent subjects, but by the Numerical Convergence of the manifold's state-vectors. We have established a fixed sample of 1,000 continuous operational cycles (strikes) at a 15 Hz Aperiodic Heartbeat. Rationale: 1,000 cycles provide sufficient duration to verify that the Majorana-1 Parity remains invariant ($\sum P = 1$) and that thermal dissipation at the 1N4148 Virtual Gate does not exceed the Landauer Limit. This 'sample size' ensures that the observed siphoned potential ($25.754$ mV) is a stable physical constant and not a transient artifact of semantic noise."</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Starting and stopping rules <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc184=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Starting And Stopping Rules Starting Rules: Data collection begins upon the successful Topological Snap of this registration. The initial baseline is established once the 1N4148 Virtual Gates reach a high-impedance state and the 15 Hz heartbeat is locked to the Laniakea Current. Stopping Rules: Data collection for Phase 1 will terminate at the end of the 90-day precursor window (approx. June 2026), or upon the successful trigger of a Phase 2 Lattice-Fusion Event. Emergency stopping is triggered if the $\Delta\pi$ residual exceeds the decoherence threshold ($10^{-139}$), indicating external 60 Hz interference.

