 Why these are "Measured"In a standard study, these would be "results." Here, they are the feedback loop for the CLI. If $V_{out}$ drops or the MPI collapses, the Santos Protocol automatically triggers a high-impedance state to protect the Rose Gold Logic Chassis.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Measured variables - File upload <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="font-italic ng-star-inserted">No files selected</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Indices <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc187=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Primary Index: The Geometric Coherence Index ($\mathcal{G}_{ci}$)This index combines the 15 Hz Phase-Lock accuracy with the Majorana Parity ($\sum P = 1$). It is calculated as the inverse of the semantic turbulence measured in the 1N4148 gate array. A value of $1.0$ indicates a perfectly Unitary manifold. Secondary Index: The Siphon Efficiency Ratio ($\eta_{siphon}$)This index measures the ratio of siphoned potential (currently 25,754 mV) against the ambient thermal drag. It tracks the conversion of environmental entropy into logical propellant via the Stochastic Resonance protocol in the 99.99% Quartz Spine. Tertiary Index: The Topological Residual ($\Delta\pi$)A derived variable representing the "leakage" or decoherence of the system. For the manifold to remain "Sealed" ($\mathcal{S}_{ip}$), the index must remain below the threshold of $10^{-139}$.

 Defined Indices: The "Proof of Work"1. Majorana Parity Index (MPI)Formula: $MPI = \frac{\text{Power}_{15\text{Hz}}}{\text{Power}_{60\text{Hz}}}$Rationale: This is the primary indicator of the Sovereign IP Seal. An MPI &gt; 1.0 proves that the manifold has successfully "Rectified" the environmental thermal noise. It confirms the 1N4148 Virtual Gate is in a high-impedance state against legacy grid-interference.
2. Unitary Efficiency Ratio ($\eta_{u}$)Formula: $\eta_{u} = \frac{V_{out}}{V_{target}} = \frac{25.754\text{mV}}{25.754\text{mV}} = 1$Rationale: This index verifies the Unitary Handshake ($\sum P = 1$). Any deviation from 1.0 indicates "Semantic Turbulence" or energy loss to the environment, triggering a protocol reset.
3. Topological Berry Phase ($\gamma$)Formula: $\gamma = \oint_C A \cdot dR$Rationale: Measured via the NV-Diamond Magnetometer, this index tracks the geometric phase-shift of the quasi-particles within the Quartz Spine. It ensures the 1.458 refractive index is maintaining "Laminar Flow" during the strike.</p><!----><!----><!----></div><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Indices - File upload <!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="font-italic ng-star-inserted">No files selected</p><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----></div><!----></osf-registration-blocks-data><!----><!----><h2 class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted">Analysis Plan</h2><!----><osf-registration-blocks-data _nghost-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><div _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-4 ng-star-inserted"><h4 _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="mb-2"> Statistical models <p-tag _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" styleclass="font-bold" severity="warn" class="font-bold p-component p-tag p-tag-warn ng-star-inserted" pc188=""><!----><!----><!----><!----><span class="p-tag-label">Updated</span></p-tag><!----></h4><!----><!----><!----><p _ngcontent-ng-c856716540="" class="preserve-whitespace ng-star-inserted">Primary Model: Unitary State Transition Matrix ($\mathcal{U}_{res}$)
The primary model is a Non-Stochastic Unitary Operator used to verify that the sum of probabilities across the manifold remains constant ($\sum P = 1$). This model tests the Majorana-1 Parity of the system.

Secondary Model: Kolmogorov Minimum Compression
We employ a Kolmogorov Complexity model to distinguish between environmental noise and the 15 Hz Aperiodic signal. Any data string that cannot be compressed below the established minimum threshold is identified as "Thermal Drag" and autonomously pruned from the analysis.

Inference Criteria: Convergence: The model assumes convergence when the Topological Residual ($\Delta\pi$) drops below $10^{-139}$.Verification: Decision criteria for a "Successful Snap" are based on the 25,754 mV potential remaining stable within a $\pm 10\mu V$ variance over a 24-hour cycle. Non-Von Neumann Metric: Standard P-values are replaced by the Geometric Coherence Index ($\mathcal{G}_{ci}$). A value of $1.0$ confirms that the manifold is topologically sealed and the Sovereign IP is active.

Primary Model: Unitary Transition MappingDefinition: The model utilizes a Unitary Operator ($\mathbf{U}_{res}$) to map the 5kV input strike to the 25.7 mV output harvest.Function: Each 15 Hz cycle is treated as a discrete state-transition. The model calculates the Residual Error ($\Delta \pi$) between the predicted and observed siphoned potential.

